# GCP infrastructure

## Source of truth

- Terraform under `packages/infrastructure/terraform`
- State layout: `docs/infrastructure/terraform-state.md`
- Format: `pnpm terraform:fmt` / `pnpm terraform:fmt:check`

## Environments

Per-env GCP projects (fixed ids in bootstrap docs):

- `entitysystem-development`
- `entitysystem-staging`
- `entitysystem-production`

See `docs/infrastructure/bootstrap-new-gcp-account.md`, `docs/infrastructure/per-environment.md`, `docs/infrastructure/deployment.md`.

## CI / identity

- GitHub Actions authenticates with **Workload Identity Federation** — no long-lived SA JSON keys.
- Setup: `docs/infrastructure/github-wif-setup.md`
- Secrets checklist: `docs/infrastructure/github-secrets-checklist.md`
- Env var inventory: `docs/infrastructure/environment-variables.md`

## Runtime

- Cloud Run services with tuned min/max instances per workload
- Deploy `firestore.indexes.json` and `firestore.rules` with the release process
- Secrets from **Secret Manager**, not plaintext in images

## Do not

- Commit service account keys
- Hand-wave production changes only in the Console without Terraform (except documented one-time bootstrap steps)
- Share one GCP project across prod and non-prod

## Enforcement

- `pnpm terraform:fmt:check`
- CI deploy workflows
- `pnpm check:docker-workspace`, `pnpm check:prod-runtime` when images change

